<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konrad I of Masovia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1187–1247</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Konrad of Masovia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konrad I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> was a Polish duke of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast dynasty</a>, ruling Masovia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a> and briefly holding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a>. Unable to stop raids by the pagan Prussians, he invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and granted it the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno">Chełmno</a> land around 1226. The Order then conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and built a powerful state that later became a long-standing rival of Poland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-masovia.jpg" alt="Konrad I of Masovia" width="167" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich A. Vossberg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KOnrad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
